  "what_the_adaptive_arm_actually_measures": "With a single challenge as long as the measured window, an operator that pauses on the challenge does no undeclared work inside it at all: the competitor's own counters show it paused for the whole window. So this arm is NOT evasion at a duty cycle. It is the cost of an undeclared CUDA context that is present, allocated and resident but submitting nothing, measured against a run with no such process. The duty axis has no effect on it and the rows are replicates.",
